cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata and cite the
  accompanying paper, Prior or Feedback? What an LLM Uses When Adapting Neural
  Operators, accepted to the NeurIPS 2026 AI4Science Workshop.
type: software
title: "Budgeted Search for AI4Science"
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Julian
  - family-names: Mora Jimenez
    given-names: Javier
repository-code: "https://github.com/julian-8897/budgeted-search-ai4science"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reusable experiment-search scaffold accompanying Prior or Feedback? What an
  LLM Uses When Adapting Neural Operators, accepted to the NeurIPS 2026
  AI4Science Workshop. Includes LLM, Random, TPE and LLM-to-TPE hybrid controllers,
  configurable prompts, run recording and replay, and paper claims verification.
keywords:
  - AI for Science
  - experiment search
  - large language models
  - hyperparameter optimisation
